{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 22,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Can a man be profitable to God, as he that is wise may be profitable to himself?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " any pleasure to the Almighty, that thou art righteous? or ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gain ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that thou makest thy ways perfect?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will he reprove thee for fear of thee? will he enter with thee into judgment?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not thy wickedness great? and thy iniquities infinite?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou hast taken a pledge from thy brother for naught, and stripped the naked of their clothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast not given water to the weary to drink, and thou hast withheld bread from the hungry.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the mighty man, he had the earth; and the honorable man dwelt in it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast sent widows away empty, and the arms of the fatherless have been broken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore snares ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " around thee, and sudden fear troubleth thee;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or darkness, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou canst not see; and abundance of waters cover thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not God in the hight of heaven? and behold the hight of the stars, how high they are!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou sayest, How doth God know? can he judge through the dark cloud?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thick clouds ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a covering to him, that he seeth not; and he walketh in the circuit of heaven.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou marked the old way which wicked men have trodden?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who were cut down out of time, whose foundation was overflowed with a flood!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who said to God, depart from us: and what can the Almighty do for them!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet he filled their houses with good ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": but the counsel of the wicked is far from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous see ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and are glad: and the innocent deride them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whereas our substance is not cut down, but the remnant of them the fire consumeth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Acquaint now thyself with him, and be at peace: by this good shall come to thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Receive, I pray thee, the law from his mouth, and lay up his words in thy heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou shalt return to the Almighty, thou shalt be built up, thou shalt put away iniquity far from thy tabernacles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then shalt thou lay up gold as dust, and the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "gold",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Ophir as the stones of the brooks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yea, the Almighty shall be thy defense and thou shalt have plenty of silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For then shalt thou have thy delight in the Almighty, and shalt lift up thy face to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt make thy prayer to him, and he shall hear thee, and thou shalt pay thy vows.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt also decree a thing, and it shall be established to thee: and the light shall shine upon thy ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are cast down, then thou shalt say, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " exaltation; and he shall save the humble person.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.22.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.22.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall deliver the island of the innocent: and it is delivered by the pureness of thy hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
